@tradition garden-hour
// Garden hour (weekly, seat 15). Moved from the plan's Wednesday 18:00 to Monday 17:30, so it never sits on Deck 3 at
// the same time as Wednesday's tasting table, and Monday starts the week with the beds tended. Volunteers after the day
// shift; the gardeners show them what to do. Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 437
title: Garden hour
when: weekly monday
at: 17:30-18:30
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 3 pool garden-tend
where: 3 pool garden
hold: 1
who: cruz-tove always, gardener 85%, garden-lover 60%, everyone 10%
anim: water
host: cruz-tove
from: cruz-tove
ties: garden tend
invite: host=cruz-tove odds=25% line="Garden hour after shift. Spare hands for the beans? They've got ambitions."

== mail
- Garden hour tomorrow, {time}, in the hydroponics garden: watering, tying in and a bit of weeding. No experience needed. The tomatoes won't judge.

== ask
- Garden hour after shift. Best way to start a week, honestly.   #warm
- I'm off to the garden at half five. The beans need tying in again.
- Garden hour later. Nothing smells as good as the garden after watering.   #warm

== here
- Water at the roots, not the leaves.
- Look, the new ones have come up. Tiny!   #warm
- Hand me the twine? This one's wandering off again.

== thanks
- You spend an hour with your hands in the beds. {host} shows you how to pinch out a tomato.   #warm
- You water a row of greens and tie in a bean that was making a run for it.   #funny

== chatter
- I tied in a bean at garden hour and now I feel responsible for it.   #funny
- Garden hour is the only hour of the week nobody talks about engines.
- The garden always looks its best the day after garden hour.
